30,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no, whole-building lets are risky if people cancel! And traveling far is way too expensive. Maybe staying local is better?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems that staying together in one place is the only way to get the different year-groups to talk. We must prioritize that.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Public bookings are a bureaucratic nightmare, and staying on campus means we have to cook for ourselves, which is a huge burden.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that inland centers have eight people to a room! That sounds like a nightmare for sleeping. We need something better.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, you're right. The transport costs are huge when we go far, and the non-refundable deposits for lodges are a financial risk we can't afford.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! If we go to a lodge, the people who stay might end up paying for those who quit. That's not fair.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"But if we stay on campus, will they actually spend time together? I worry we will just go home to our own rooms.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, the workload is the issue. If we stay on campus, the organizers are stuck in the kitchen. We need a place with staff.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Rin,,But the public beds are cheap! Though eight people in a room sounds like no one will sleep. What about a lodge?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Misaki,,A lodge is too expensive and risky. We need to balance the budget and the workload without bankrupting the club account.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we stay on campus, it's the cheapest, right? But @Ryuji is worried about the cooking. Is there a middle ground?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"If we want the members to stay and bond, we need a place that feels like a getaway, not just more school.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The public center is too much paperwork and the rooms are cramped. The campus is too much work. The lodge is the only one with staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want to be tired again! If the inland place is too crowded, maybe the lodge is the only way to actually rest?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Misaki,,The lodge's fixed headcount is a dealbreaker for me. We cannot risk more budget gaps. We should look at the campus or public options.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm leaning towards the campus then, as long as we can figure out the food. It's the safest for everyone's money.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I fear the campus won't fix the social divide. But if the lodge is too risky, perhaps the public center?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The public center's lottery is a gamble. If we fail, we have nothing. Campus is guaranteed, but the labor is high.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just want a bed where I can actually sleep! If the public center is too crowded, I'm voting against it.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Let's consider the options carefully. Campus is cheap but hard work. Public is cheap but cramped. Lodge is comfortable but expensive and risky.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
